        "description": "\"Leathers\" opens the album with an extended atmospheric intro — feedback, ambient guitars, no drums — before exploding into one of the heaviest grooves on the record. Abe's entrance is a moment: a single crash, then a locked-in, half-time pocket that drives the rest of the song.\n\nThe verse pattern is built around syncopated kick hits and a steady backbeat, leaving plenty of room for Chino's vocal melody. The chorus shifts to straight eighth notes with crash accents on every downbeat — classic Abe contrast.\n\nWhat makes the drum part work is the patience. Abe doesn't add fills until the second chorus. He doesn't open the hi-hats until the bridge. Every dynamic choice is earned, which is why the song's climactic ending hits as hard as it does.",
