        "description": "\"Entombed\" is the album's most atmospheric track — a six-minute slow dance that drifts more than it drives. Abe's drumming here is almost ambient, with hi-hat textures, occasional rim clicks, and a kick pattern that feels more like a heartbeat than a groove.\n\nThe genius is in the restraint. For the first three minutes, Abe plays almost nothing — and that nothing is essential. The song's atmosphere depends on the drums staying out of the way, supporting the dream-state mood rather than asserting themselves.\n\nWhen the kit finally enters more fully, the contrast is devastating. Suddenly the song has weight and forward motion, and the listener feels it because they've been waiting for it. This is dynamic patience at its most extreme.",
