        "description": "Closing the album proper, \"Rosemary\" is a seven-minute exploration that combines the dream-state textures of \"Entombed\" with the cathartic releases of \"Tempest.\" Abe's drumming threads the needle between atmosphere and impact.\n\nThe verse groove is sparse — kick, rim click, occasional snare — leaving room for the song's harmonic depth to register. The chorus opens up with a full backbeat and open hi-hats, but never overplays its hand.\n\nThe extended outro features Abe locked into a repetitive groove while layers build around him. He doesn't \"improve\" the pattern. He doesn't add fills. He just plays the same thing, beautifully, while the song resolves around him. That kind of discipline is what separates great drummers from busy ones.",
